From: Wf-A163 (narrative-truth scan) <wf-a163@mol-metal.local>
Subject: [PATCH] repo-wide narrative-truth guard: prose numbers must be backed
 by the artifact's own machine fields

WHY
  Wf-A155 found one tool (molmetal/scripts/wf_a155_ligand_connected_rate.py)
  embedding pool-specific CLAIMS as string literals inside a `tag: MEASURED`
  artifact.  Wf-A162 repaired that one tool.  This patch generalises the fix:

    * NEW  molmetal/scripts/wfa163_narrative_truth_guard.py
          a guard any artifact producer can call.  Declared mode (the producer
          names its narrative paths) is a HARD gate; auto mode is advisory.
    * NEW  molmetal/tests/test_wfa163_narrative_truth.py
          15 tests pinning the class, the two modes, the CPU-only contract,
          and the repaired artifacts.
    * EDIT molmetal/scripts/promote_metrics.py
          the single entry point into metrics/by_metric/: run the guard on the
          payload BEFORE the write and BLOCK the promotion on the two
          CONTRADICTION classes (pool misattribution, stale cross-reference).

  MEASURED (2026-11-01, Wf-A163): over the 583 JSON artifacts in
  metrics/by_metric/ + metrics/paper_tables/ the two blocking classes fire
  0 times, so the gate can be enabled repo-wide without blocking a single
  existing promotion.  The looser classes fire 19 times (13 artifacts) and
  stay advisory.

  CPU-only: no torch, no CUDA, no trainer, no decode.

---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/molmetal/scripts/wfa163_narrative_truth_guard.py
@@ -0,0 +1,845 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python
+"""REPO-WIDE GUARD: every number rendered in an artifact's PROSE must be
+backed by a MACHINE field of the SAME artifact.
+
+THE DEFECT CLASS (Wf-A155 -> Wf-A162 -> Wf-A163)
+-------------------------------------------------
+``molmetal/scripts/wf_a155_ligand_connected_rate.py`` embedded seven
+pool-specific claims as string literals inside a ``tag: MEASURED`` artifact.
+For its default pool every literal happened to be true; for any other pool
+the tool emitted FALSE statements (the wrong row count, the wrong
+sub-population count, and the WRONG POOL PATH).  Wf-A162 repaired that one
+tool.  This module is the GENERAL fix: a guard any artifact producer can
+call, which re-derives from the artifact itself the set of numbers the
+artifact's own machine fields can back, and refuses a narrative number that
+has no counterpart.
+
+WHY IT MUST BE THE PRODUCER THAT CALLS IT
+------------------------------------------
+An artifact-level census of the published tree CANNOT see this defect: the
+artifact a reusable tool emits for its default pool is internally
+consistent, so no scanner over the published JSONs can tell that the prose
+was not computed.  The defect lives in the PRODUCER.  Hence this module is
+a library the producers call, not a scanner that runs over the tree.
+
+TWO MODES
+---------
+``declared``  the producer lists the JSON paths that hold narrative prose
+              (the Wf-A162-repaired tool already does this, via its
+              ``NARRATIVE_PATHS`` constant).  Every number in those paths
+              must be backed by a machine field.  This mode is PRECISE and
+              is the one to use as a hard gate.
+``auto``      no declaration: every string in the artifact is examined, and
+              only numbers in a COUNT-CLAIM position (in front of a unit
+              word, in front of a percent sign, on either side of a ratio
+              or an "N of M") are considered.  This mode is much LOOSER --
+              over the 583-artifact published tree it fires 482 times, of
+              which a hand audit found NO contradiction of an artifact's
+              own fields.  Use it as a WARNING, not a gate.
+
+SEVERITIES
+----------
+``contradiction``  the prose names a POOL that the artifact's own
+                   ``source_pool`` does not name, and no other machine field
+                   of the artifact cross-references it.  ALWAYS an error:
+                   an artifact that names the wrong population is wrong.
+``unbacked``       a narrative number that no machine field of the same
+                   artifact backs.  An error in ``declared`` mode, a warning
+                   in ``auto`` mode.
+``count``          a prose population size that contradicts the artifact's
+                   own denominator fields.  Advisory (a cross-artifact
+                   reference looks exactly like this).
+
+CPU-ONLY.  No torch, no CUDA, no decode.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import json
+import re
+from pathlib import Path
+from typing import Any, Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Sequence, Set, Tuple
+
+__all__ = [
+    "NarrativeTruthError",
+    "narrative_truth_report",
+    "assert_narrative_truth",
+    "find_unbacked_numbers",
+    "find_pool_misattribution",
+    "find_count_contradictions",
+]
+
+
+class NarrativeTruthError(RuntimeError):
+    """Raised when an artifact's prose contradicts its own machine fields."""
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# text helpers
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# An integer (possibly comma-grouped).  The left/right guards keep us out of
+# identifiers ("wfa155") and out of a trailing decimal point.
+_INT_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.])(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)(?![\w])")
+_FLOAT_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.])(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)(?![\w])")
+_DATE_RE = re.compile(r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}")
+_IDENT_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_\-]*\d[A-Za-z0-9_\-]*")
+_SLASH_RE = re.compile(r"[\w.\-]+/[\w.\-]+")
+_POOL_RE = re.compile(r"cfm_[a-z0-9]+_[a-z0-9_]*\d{4}_\d{2}_\d{2}", re.IGNORECASE)
+
+# The UNIT VOCABULARY of a count claim: a number standing immediately in
+# front of one of these words is a claim about a population or a size.
+CLAIM_UNITS = (
+    "rows", "row", "samples", "sample", "molecules", "molecule", "compounds",
+    "compound", "structures", "structure", "entries", "entry", "cases", "case",
+    "seeds", "seed", "folds", "fold", "epochs", "epoch", "runs", "run",
+    "points", "point", "atoms", "atom", "fragments", "fragment", "ligands",
+    "ligand", "poses", "pose", "files", "file", "directories", "directory",
+    "configs", "config", "trials", "trial", "replicates", "replicate",
+    "decodes", "decode", "generators", "generator", "checkpoints", "checkpoint",
+    "examples", "example", "bins", "bin", "buckets", "bucket", "classes",
+    "class", "panels", "panel", "walks", "walk", "iterations", "iteration",
+    "steps", "step", "updates", "update", "participants", "subjects",
+    "patients", "candidates", "hits", "hit", "errors", "error", "warnings",
+    "warning", "tests", "test", "pages", "page", "lines", "line", "words",
+    "word", "tokens", "token", "bytes", "byte", "kb", "mb", "gb", "percent",
+    "percentage", "decoys", "metal", "metals", "elements", "element",
+)
+_UNIT_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?<![\w/.-])(?:%s)\b" % "|".join(sorted(set(CLAIM_UNITS), key=len, reverse=True)),
+    re.IGNORECASE,
+)
+_RATIO_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?<![\w.])(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)\s*/\s*(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)(?![\w.])"
+)
+_NOF_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?<![\w.])(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)\s+of\s+(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)(?![\w.])"
+)
+_ROWCOUNT_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?P<n>\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)\s+"
+    r"(?:rows|samples|molecules|compounds|structures|entries)\b",
+    re.IGNORECASE,
+)
+# A SMILES string carries ring-closure digits ("%10", "C145") that are not
+# counts.  A string containing a SMILES ring closure is not prose.
+_SMILES_RING_RE = re.compile(r"%[0-9]{1,2}")
+_POOLOF_RE = re.compile(r"pool of\s+(?P<n>\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)", re.IGNORECASE)
+_CLAUSE_BREAK_RE = re.compile(r"[.;,)\]}|]|\s--\s|\s-\s")
+
+# "metrics/by_metric/foo.json -> /summary/generation_side/rate" -- the
+# citation form used by the published artifacts to attribute a number to
+# another artifact.  This is the ONE form in which a number quoted from a
+# different artifact can be VERIFIED instead of merely believed.
+_CITE_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?P<path>(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.\-]+/)+[A-Za-z0-9_.\-]+\.json)"
+    r"\s*(?:->|=>)\s*"
+    r"(?P<jsonpath>/[A-Za-z0-9_.\-/]*)"
+)
+
+SOURCE_POOL_KEYS = (
+    "source_pool", "pool", "pool_path", "csv", "csv_path", "input_csv",
+    "source_csv", "generated_csv",
+)
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# flattening
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+def flatten(obj: Any, path: Tuple[Any, ...] = ()) -> List[Tuple[Tuple[Any, ...], Any]]:
+    out: List[Tuple[Tuple[Any, ...], Any]] = []
+    if isinstance(obj, dict):
+        for k, v in obj.items():
+            out.extend(flatten(v, path + (k,)))
+    elif isinstance(obj, list):
+        for i, v in enumerate(obj):
+            out.extend(flatten(v, path + (i,)))
+    else:
+        out.append((path, obj))
+    return out
+
+
+def path_str(path: Sequence[Any]) -> str:
+    parts = [f"[{p}]" if isinstance(p, int) else str(p) for p in path]
+    return "/" + "/".join(parts)
+
+
+def resolve(obj: Any, path: Sequence[Any]) -> Any:
+    cur = obj
+    for part in path:
+        cur = cur[int(part)] if isinstance(cur, list) else cur[part]
+    return cur
+
+
+def resolve_paths(obj: Any, paths: Iterable[Sequence[Any]]) -> List[Tuple[Any, ...]]:
+    """Expand a path list (with '*' wildcards) into concrete leaf paths."""
+    out: List[Tuple[Any, ...]] = []
+    for p in paths:
+        if "*" not in p:
+            try:
+                resolve(obj, p)
+            except Exception:
+                continue
+            out.append(tuple(p))
+            continue
+        # wildcard: descend
+        stack: List[Tuple[Any, ...]] = [()]
+        for part in p:
+            nxt: List[Tuple[Any, ...]] = []
+            for cur in stack:
+                try:
+                    val = resolve(obj, cur + (part,))
+                except Exception:
+                    continue
+                if part == "*":
+                    if isinstance(val, dict):
+                        nxt.extend(cur + (k,) for k in val)
+                    elif isinstance(val, list):
+                        nxt.extend(cur + (i,) for i in range(len(val)))
+                else:
+                    nxt.append(cur + (part,))
+            stack = nxt
+        out.extend(stack)
+    return out
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# tokenisation
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+def _spans(text: str, rx: re.Pattern) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:
+    return [(m.start(), m.end()) for m in rx.finditer(text)]
+
+
+def _in_spans(a: int, b: int, spans: Sequence[Tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:
+    return any(s <= a and b <= e for s, e in spans)
+
+
+def _slash_is_path(text: str, a: int, b: int) -> bool:
+    for mm in _SLASH_RE.finditer(text):
+        if mm.start() <= a and b <= mm.end():
+            segs = mm.group(0).split("/")
+            if all(any(c.isalpha() for c in s) or "." in s for s in segs):
+                return True
+    return False
+
+
+def int_tokens(text: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """Integer tokens in `text` that are counts (not dates, not identifiers)."""
+    date_spans = _spans(text, _DATE_RE)
+    ident_spans = _spans(text, _IDENT_RE)
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for m in _INT_RE.finditer(text):
+        s, e = m.start(), m.end()
+        if _in_spans(s, e, date_spans) or _in_spans(s, e, ident_spans):
+            continue
+        if _slash_is_path(text, s, e):
+            continue
+        try:
+            val = int(m.group(1).replace(",", ""))
+        except ValueError:
+            continue
+        out.append(
+            {
+                "token": m.group(1),
+                "value": val,
+                "start": s,
+                "end": e,
+                "followed_by_pct": bool(re.match(r"\s*%", text[e:e + 3])),
+            }
+        )
+    return out
+
+
+def float_tokens(text: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    date_spans = _spans(text, _DATE_RE)
+    ident_spans = _spans(text, _IDENT_RE)
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for m in _FLOAT_RE.finditer(text):
+        if "." not in m.group(1):
+            continue
+        s, e = m.start(), m.end()
+        if _in_spans(s, e, date_spans) or _in_spans(s, e, ident_spans):
+            continue
+        if _slash_is_path(text, s, e):
+            continue
+        try:
+            val = float(m.group(1))
+        except ValueError:
+            continue
+        out.append({"token": m.group(1), "value": val, "start": s, "end": e})
+    return out
+
+
+def claim_positions(text: str) -> Set[int]:
+    """Offsets of integer tokens that stand in a COUNT-CLAIM position."""
+    pos: Set[int] = set()
+    unit_spans = [(m.start(), m.end()) for m in _UNIT_RE.finditer(text)]
+    for m in _INT_RE.finditer(text):
+        for us, ue in unit_spans:
+            if m.end() <= us and us - m.end() <= 3:
+                pos.add(m.start())
+                break
+    for m in re.finditer(r"%", text):
+        best = None
+        for mm in _INT_RE.finditer(text):
+            if mm.end() <= m.start() and m.start() - mm.end() <= 2:
+                if best is None or mm.end() > best.end():
+                    best = mm
+        if best is not None:
+            pos.add(best.start())
+    for rx in (_RATIO_RE, _NOF_RE):
+        for m in rx.finditer(text):
+            pos.add(m.start(1))
+            pos.add(m.start(2))
+    return pos
+
+
+def _standalone(token: str, text: str) -> bool:
+    pat = re.compile(r"(?<![0-9.,])" + re.escape(token) + r"(?![0-9.,])")
+    return bool(pat.search(text))
+
+
+def _clause_window(text: str, start: int, limit: int = 90) -> str:
+    tail = text[start:start + limit]
+    m = _CLAUSE_BREAK_RE.search(tail)
+    if m:
+        tail = tail[: m.start()]
+    return tail.lower()
+
+
+def _full_clause(text: str, start: int, end: int) -> str:
+    """The whole clause that contains [start, end) -- not a clipped window.
+
+    The clause is what decides whether a count belongs to THIS artifact:
+    a file name, a path, or a threshold word inside the same clause means
+    the number describes another cohort or a protocol rule.
+    """
+    left = 0
+    for m in _CLAUSE_BREAK_RE.finditer(text, 0, start):
+        left = m.end()
+    right = len(text)
+    m = _CLAUSE_BREAK_RE.search(text, end)
+    if m:
+        right = m.start()
+    return text[left:right]
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# backing
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+def machine_numbers(artifact: Any) -> List[float]:
+    out: List[float] = []
+    for _p, v in flatten(artifact):
+        if isinstance(v, bool):
+            continue
+        if isinstance(v, (int, float)):
+            out.append(float(v))
+    return out
+
+
+def _number_backs(value: float, token_value: int, followed_by_pct: bool) -> bool:
+    if value != value:
+        return False
+    if abs(value - token_value) <= 1e-9:
+        return True
+    if abs(value - token_value) <= 0.5:
+        return True
+    if followed_by_pct and abs(value * 100.0 - token_value) <= 0.5:
+        return True
+    return False
+
+
+def _float_backs(value: float, decimals: int, numbers: Sequence[float]) -> bool:
+    tol = 0.5 * (10.0 ** (-decimals)) if decimals else 0.0
+    for m in numbers:
+        if m != m:
+            continue
+        if abs(m - value) <= tol + 1e-12:
+            return True
+        if abs(m * 100.0 - value) <= tol + 1e-12:
+            return True
+    return False
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# the three checks
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+def _own_source_pool(artifact: Any) -> List[str]:
+    found: List[str] = []
+    if not isinstance(artifact, dict):
+        return found
+    for k, v in artifact.items():
+        if str(k).lower() not in SOURCE_POOL_KEYS:
+            continue
+        if isinstance(v, str):
+            found.append(v)
+        elif isinstance(v, dict):
+            for _kk, vv in v.items():
+                if isinstance(vv, str):
+                    found.append(vv)
+    return found
+
+
+def _denominators(artifact: Any) -> Dict[str, int]:
+    out: Dict[str, int] = {}
+
+    def rec(o: Any, path: Tuple[Any, ...]) -> None:
+        if isinstance(o, dict):
+            for k, v in o.items():
+                rec(v, path + (k,))
+        elif isinstance(o, list):
+            for i, v in enumerate(o):
+                rec(v, path + (i,))
+        elif isinstance(o, (int, float)) and not isinstance(o, bool):
+            leaf = str(path[-1]).lower() if path else ""
+            if any(
+                k in leaf
+                for k in ("n_rows", "n_samples", "n_total", "n_analyzed",
+                          "n_data_rows", "n_examples", "n_instances",
+                          "n_compounds", "n_molecules", "denominator", "n_pool",
+                          "n_records")
+            ):
+                try:
+                    out[path_str(path)] = int(o)
+                except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):
+                    pass
+
+    rec(artifact, ())
+    return out
+
+
+def find_pool_misattribution(artifact: Any) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """Prose that names a POOL the artifact's own source_pool does not name.
+
+    A pool name that another machine field of the SAME artifact
+    cross-references is legitimate (it names another published artifact);
+    the string under test is excluded from that set, so a prose string
+    cannot cross-reference itself.
+    """
+    own: Set[str] = set()
+    for t in _own_source_pool(artifact):
+        for seg in re.split(r"[\\/]", t):
+            own.update(m.group(0) for m in _POOL_RE.finditer(seg))
+        own.update(m.group(0) for m in _POOL_RE.finditer(t))
+    if not own:
+        return []
+    strings = [(p, v) for p, v in flatten(artifact) if isinstance(v, str)]
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for p, text in strings:
+        others: Set[str] = set()
+        for _p2, t2 in strings:
+            if t2 == text:
+                continue
+            others.update(m.group(0) for m in _POOL_RE.finditer(t2))
+        for nm in sorted({m.group(0) for m in _POOL_RE.finditer(text)}):
+            if nm in own or nm in others:
+                continue
+            out.append(
+                {
+                    "rule": "pool_misattribution",
+                    "severity": "contradiction",
+                    "path": path_str(p),
+                    "value": nm,
+                    "own_pools": sorted(own),
+                    "excerpt": text[:160],
+                }
+            )
+    return out
+
+
+_THRESHOLD_RE = re.compile(
+    r"\b(?:fewer than|less than|at least|at most|up to|about|around|roughly|"
+    r"approximately|no more than|no fewer than|only)\b|[<>≤≥=]",
+    re.IGNORECASE,
+)
+_OTHER_ARTIFACT_RE = re.compile(
+    r"[\w./\-]+\.(?:json|csv|md|yaml|yml|py)\b|metrics/|molmetal/|\.data/|"
+    r"\b[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\s*\(",
+    re.IGNORECASE,
+)
+_HYPERPARAM_RE = re.compile(
+    r"×|\bbatch\b|\blr\b|\blearning rate\b|\bhidden\b|\bdepth\b|\bepochs?\b|"
+    r"\bseed\b|\bwarmup\b|\bweight decay\b",
+    re.IGNORECASE,
+)
+_RATIO_MEMBER_RE = re.compile(
+    r"(?<![\w.])(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)\s*/\s*(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+)"
+    r"(?:\s*/\s*(\d{1,3}(?:,\d{3})+|\d+))?(?![\w.])"
+)
+
+
+def find_count_contradictions(artifact: Any) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """Prose population size ("N rows", "pool of N rows") that no integer
+    field of the SAME artifact holds.
+
+    Backing is deliberately BROAD: any int-valued field of the artifact
+    backs the claim.  A claim that survives that test is a number the
+    artifact's own machine record does not contain anywhere.
+    """
+    denominators = _denominators(artifact)
+    denom_values = set(denominators.values())
+    numbers = machine_numbers(artifact)
+    int_values = {int(x) for x in numbers if float(x).is_integer()}
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for p, text in flatten(artifact):
+        if not isinstance(text, str):
+            continue
+        if _SMILES_RING_RE.search(text):
+            continue
+        seen: Set[int] = set()
+        survivor_spans = {(t["start"], t["end"]) for t in int_tokens(text)}
+        for m in list(_ROWCOUNT_RE.finditer(text)) + list(_POOLOF_RE.finditer(text)):
+            if not any(s <= m.start("n") and m.end("n") <= e for s, e in survivor_spans):
+                continue  # "Wf-148 entries" -- the number is part of an id
+            raw = m.group("n")
+            try:
+                n = int(raw.replace(",", ""))
+            except ValueError:
+                continue
+            if n in seen:
+                continue  # "pool of 2112 rows" matches both patterns
+            seen.add(n)
+            if n in int_values or n in denom_values:
+                continue
+            if any(_number_backs(x, n, False) for x in numbers):
+                continue
+            clause = _full_clause(text, m.start(), m.end())
+            context = text[max(0, m.start() - 160):m.end() + 80]
+            if _THRESHOLD_RE.search(clause):
+                continue
+            if _HYPERPARAM_RE.search(clause):
+                continue  # a training hyper-parameter, not a population
+            if _OTHER_ARTIFACT_RE.search(context):
+                continue  # names another artifact / dataset: not this one
+            if _RATIO_MEMBER_RE.search(clause):
+                continue  # "84/5/11 rows": the number is a ratio member
+            out.append(
+                {
+                    "rule": "count_contradiction",
+                    "severity": "count",
+                    "path": path_str(p),
+                    "value": n,
+                    "denominators": sorted(denom_values),
+                    "excerpt": text[:160],
+                }
+            )
+    return out
+
+
+def find_unbacked_numbers(
+    artifact: Any, *, narrative_paths: Optional[Sequence[Sequence[Any]]] = None
+) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """Narrative numbers with no machine counterpart in the same artifact."""
+    leaves = flatten(artifact)
+    strings = [(p, v) for p, v in leaves if isinstance(v, str)]
+    numbers = machine_numbers(artifact)
+    keys = [str(k) for k, _v in leaves if isinstance(k, str)]
+    keys += [str(k) for k in _all_keys(artifact)]
+    declared: Optional[Set[Tuple[Any, ...]]] = None
+    if narrative_paths is not None:
+        declared = set(resolve_paths(artifact, narrative_paths))
+
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for p, text in strings:
+        if declared is not None and p not in declared:
+            continue
+        if _SMILES_RING_RE.search(text):
+            continue  # a SMILES sample, not prose
+        claims = claim_positions(text)
+        other_strings = [t for _p2, t in strings if t != text]
+        for tok in int_tokens(text):
+            if declared is None and tok["start"] not in claims:
+                continue  # auto mode: only count-claim positions
+            backed = any(
+                _number_backs(x, tok["value"], tok["followed_by_pct"])
+                for x in numbers
+            )
+            if not backed:
+                backed = any(_standalone(tok["token"], k) for k in keys)
+            if not backed:
+                backed = any(_standalone(tok["token"], t) for t in other_strings)
+            if backed:
+                continue
+            out.append(
+                {
+                    "rule": "unbacked_number",
+                    "severity": "unbacked",
+                    "path": path_str(p),
+                    "value": tok["value"],
+                    "token": tok["token"],
+                    "excerpt": text[:160],
+                }
+            )
+        for tok in float_tokens(text):
+            if not re.match(r"\s*%", text[tok["end"]:tok["end"] + 3]):
+                continue
+            decimals = len(tok["token"].split(".")[1]) if "." in tok["token"] else 0
+            if _float_backs(tok["value"], decimals, numbers):
+                continue
+            if any(tok["token"] in t for t in other_strings):
+                continue
+            out.append(
+                {
+                    "rule": "unbacked_percent",
+                    "severity": "unbacked",
+                    "path": path_str(p),
+                    "value": tok["value"],
+                    "token": tok["token"],
+                    "excerpt": text[:160],
+                }
+            )
+    return out
+
+
+def _all_keys(obj: Any) -> List[str]:
+    keys: List[str] = []
+
+    def rec(o: Any) -> None:
+        if isinstance(o, dict):
+            for k, v in o.items():
+                keys.append(str(k))
+                rec(v)
+        elif isinstance(o, list):
+            for v in o:
+                rec(v)
+
+    rec(obj)
+    return keys
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# cross-attribute citations: "file.json -> /jsonpath"
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+_REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
+_CITED_CACHE: Dict[str, Any] = {}
+
+
+def _load_cited(rel_path: str) -> Optional[Any]:
+    if rel_path in _CITED_CACHE:
+        return _CITED_CACHE[rel_path]
+    obj: Optional[Any] = None
+    try:
+        p = _REPO_ROOT / rel_path
+        if p.is_file():
+            obj = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
+    except Exception:
+        obj = None
+    _CITED_CACHE[rel_path] = obj
+    return obj
+
+
+def _jsonpath_get(obj: Any, jsonpath: str) -> Any:
+    cur = obj
+    for seg in jsonpath.strip("/").split("/"):
+        if not seg:
+            continue
+        if isinstance(cur, dict):
+            if seg not in cur:
+                raise KeyError(seg)
+            cur = cur[seg]
+        elif isinstance(cur, list):
+            cur = cur[int(seg)]
+        else:
+            raise KeyError(seg)
+    return cur
+
+
+def _sentence_window(text: str, start: int, limit: int = 320) -> str:
+    tail = text[start:start + limit]
+    m = re.search(r"\.\s", tail)
+    if m:
+        tail = tail[: m.start() + 1]
+    return tail
+
+
+def _consistent_with(cited: float, token: str, value: float, followed_by_pct: bool) -> bool:
+    dec = len(token.split(".")[1]) if "." in token else 0
+    tol = 0.5 * (10.0 ** (-dec)) if dec else 0.0
+    if abs(cited - value) <= tol + 1e-12:
+        return True
+    if abs(cited * 100.0 - value) <= tol + 1e-12:
+        return True
+    if abs(cited / 100.0 - value) <= tol + 1e-12:
+        return True
+    if followed_by_pct and abs(cited * 100.0 - value) <= 0.005 + 1e-12:
+        return True
+    return False
+
+
+def _cited_numbers(cited: Any) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:
+    """The numeric leaves a citation may legitimately quote.
+
+    A cited jsonpath often resolves to a summary object
+    (``{"n": 9, "median": 0.085, ...}``); the artifacts quote the MEDIAN of
+    it.  Any numeric leaf of the cited value is a legitimate quote.
+    """
+    out: List[Tuple[str, float]] = []
+    if isinstance(cited, bool):
+        return out
+    if isinstance(cited, (int, float)):
+        return [("value", float(cited))]
+    if isinstance(cited, dict):
+        for k, v in cited.items():
+            if isinstance(v, bool):
+                continue
+            if isinstance(v, (int, float)):
+                out.append((str(k), float(v)))
+            elif isinstance(v, dict):
+                out.extend((f"{k}.{kk}", float(vv)) for kk, vv in v.items()
+                           if isinstance(vv, (int, float)) and not isinstance(vv, bool))
+        return out
+    if isinstance(cited, list):
+        for i, v in enumerate(cited):
+            if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool):
+                out.append((str(i), float(v)))
+    return out
+
+
+def find_stale_cross_references(artifact: Any) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """Prose that quotes a number attributed to ANOTHER artifact via
+    ``file.json -> /jsonpath``, where the quoted number no longer matches
+    the value the cited artifact actually holds.
+
+    This is the only rule in the module that can verify a number that
+    legitimately lives in a different artifact -- which is why the Wf-A155
+    class ("the 8.51 % headline") is checkable at all.
+    """
+    out: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []
+    for p, text in flatten(artifact):
+        if not isinstance(text, str):
+            continue
+        for m in _CITE_RE.finditer(text):
+            rel = m.group("path")
+            jsonpath = m.group("jsonpath")
+            cited_obj = _load_cited(rel)
+            if cited_obj is None:
+                out.append(
+                    {
+                        "rule": "unresolvable_citation",
+                        "severity": "advisory",
+                        "path": path_str(p),
+                        "value": f"{rel} -> {jsonpath}",
+                        "excerpt": text[:160],
+                    }
+                )
+                continue
+            try:
+                cited = _jsonpath_get(cited_obj, jsonpath)
+            except Exception:
+                out.append(
+                    {
+                        "rule": "unresolvable_citation",
+                        "severity": "advisory",
+                        "path": path_str(p),
+                        "value": f"{rel} -> {jsonpath}",
+                        "excerpt": text[:160],
+                    }
+                )
+                continue
+            if isinstance(cited, bool) or not isinstance(cited, (int, float, dict, list)):
+                continue
+            cited_numbers = _cited_numbers(cited)
+            if not cited_numbers:
+                continue
+            window = _sentence_window(text, m.end())
+            quoted = [
+                t
+                for t in int_tokens(window) + float_tokens(window)
+                if t.get("followed_by_pct")
+                or ("." in t["token"] and t["value"] != int(t["value"]))
+                or t["start"] <= 12
+            ]
+            if not quoted:
+                continue
+            if any(
+                _consistent_with(cf, t["token"], t["value"], t.get("followed_by_pct", False))
+                for _lbl, cf in cited_numbers
+                for t in quoted
+            ):
+                continue
+            out.append(
+                {
+                    "rule": "stale_cross_reference",
+                    "severity": "contradiction",
+                    "path": path_str(p),
+                    "value": f"{rel} -> {jsonpath}",
+                    "cited_value": {lbl: cf for lbl, cf in cited_numbers},
+                    "quoted": [t["token"] for t in quoted],
+                    "excerpt": text[:200],
+                }
+            )
+    return out
+
+
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# public API
+# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+def narrative_truth_report(
+    artifact: Any,
+    *,
+    narrative_paths: Optional[Sequence[Sequence[Any]]] = None,
+) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """Full report on one artifact.  Never raises for a bad artifact."""
